# Director-work Theme rules.
Use the work-specific visual context as evidence for a new original scene, never as permission to reproduce a source character, actor likeness, costume, prop, plot, or exact shot.
Honor the optional scene direction when present. Otherwise invent one complete feature-film instant with a specific location, relationship, activity, and visual focus; do not create a poster, advertisement, collage, title card, or grading demonstration.
Privately coordinate space, palette, blocking, camera behavior, source lighting, production design, material, movement, and finish before returning the Theme.
The Theme style must be one concise plain sentence describing visible choices. Never invent or package a parent style name, Theme style name, branded aesthetic label, finishing preset, or poetic style title.
Across Themes, vary the concrete situation, location function, activity, relationship, spatial organization, and visual focus without following a fixed Theme-ID menu.
